        "title": "Prove an informal first-order theorem with Vampire ATP",
        "action_ids": [
          "atp:demo"
        ]
      }
    },
    "mathformer.native_boundary": {
      "execution": "Each MCP block calls the same native controller helper as run_intent_match; run_action retains the full native scientific subprocess and write audit.",
      "registry": "Caller-supplied registry projection is checked against build_registry and passed to both run_action and finish; no caller-supplied executable definitions.",
      "selection": "Already selected match; score and matched_terms are retained while source route metadata is restored from build_intent_routes.",
      "loop_bound": "Exact one-action specialization, constrained by RouteMatch; exhaustion is unreachable for a conforming advance result.",
      "failure_policy": "Always aggregate returned ok=false; do not raise before append/finish. Exceptions still propagate.",
      "scientific_payloads": "HubResult is the transport envelope; scientific reports and proof files remain native artifacts.",
      "limits": "The prior 3600-second/one-operation declarations were not native global budgets. Five calls accounts for this expanded controller; 3600 remains a normalization ceiling. The native outer subprocess timeout is 120 seconds."
    },
