        "vampire_time_limit_seconds": 3,
        "subprocess_timeout_seconds": 120,
        "generation_enabled": true,
        "minimization_enabled": true
      },
      "scientific_implementation": "discover_proof drains discover_proof_steps. Generate formalization candidates; for each, select at most eight trusted positive-scoring premises, traverse the finite generated-lemma list, skip ineligible lemmas, prove eligible lemmas before promotion, then augment selected premises with promoted lemmas. Traverse the original augmented list once for greedy deletion, carrying current premises and minimization attempts; skip absent candidates and retain a deletion only on proof, using one-second Vampire calls. Run the final problem and persist its artifacts. Append each candidate attempt and carry the first winning problem/result/attempt; stop on first proof or candidate exhaustion, then persist discovery_report.json. Empty finite lists complete normally. No proof yields a report with ok=false and CLI exit 3. Direct attempts and generation/minimization bypasses belong to the reusable implementation; this route enables all three premise stages."
    }
